tor should handle negative numbers automatically by including the minus sign before the formatted number.\n\n```python\nreturn f\"${n:,}\"\n```\n\nThis gives:\n- 4640039 -> \"$4,640,039\" \n- -4640039 -> \"-$4,640,039\"\n\nThe format specifier `{:,.f}` should handle the comma placement automatically. However, to keep it simple and clear, I'll implement a straightforward version that works reliably across Python versions.",
